{# W3C SCXML 4.9: "If the processing of an element causes an error to be
   raised, the processor MUST NOT process the remaining elements of the
   block." A statement of a sce-static document that `forge::static_lowering`
   lowered to Rust ahead of the template (`native_code`) is emitted as it is —
   unless it can fail (`native_fails`), when it arrives as an expression that
   is `true` when it failed, `error.execution` already raised. Which block the
   error ends, and what leaves it, is known from where the statement is
   rendered, so it is decided here: `break 'action_block` inside a block that
   has that label, and nowhere to go outside one.

   The caller passes `in_action_block` because an imported macro does not see
   the includer's context. #}
{% macro emit(action, in_action_block) -%}
{% if action.native_fails and in_action_block %}
let sce_failed = {{ action.native_code }};
if sce_failed {
    break 'action_block;  // W3C SCXML 4.9: the error ends the block
}
{% elif action.native_fails %}
let _ = {{ action.native_code }};
{% else %}
{{ action.native_code }}
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
